From 80e04777480ee1f1a70121d5073099e59c2e13ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:16:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-9 first three data planes

Implement the first three batch-9 Unit data planes on top of the reconciled
canonical chain. Base in the reconciled canonical order is the 29-layer chain
through 0148 (canonical 75f1d24 plus 0120-0129, 0131, 0134, 0136, 0130, 0133,
0135, 0132, 0137, 0138, 0139, 0140, 0141, 0142, 0143, 0144, 0145, 0146, 0147
and 0148); this is the 30th layer after 0120 and it applies at the chain end.
No guest/Device Service evidence is recorded; all three stay planned.

- glass (U158): new CONTROL_UNIT_GLASS I2C slave at 0x3D with the SSD1309
  control/command/data framing (control byte 0x00 commands / 0x40 GDDRAM data),
  a page-addressed 128x64 GDDRAM framebuffer, display on/off, contrast and
  column/page commands. unit/glass.py only registers an M5Unified external
  display; the product page's internal-firmware Protocol table is unreadable,
  so the two buttons and the buzzer are only static QOM fixtures (2-bit mask /
  hex fixture) with NO claimed semantics, and transparent-OLED optics are
  NOT RUN. 0x3D conflicts with lcd/oled/mini-oled/glass2.
- rf433t (U114): PORT.B yellow=RF_TX SYN115 ASK transmitter. There is no public
  UIFlow2 Unit driver and no ASK encoding table, so only the host GPIO
  bitstream is observed (output-level, edge-count, bit-count, bitstream); RF
  433.92MHz/antenna/10dBm/range are NOT RUN.
- rf433r (U113): PORT.B white=RF_RX SYN531R ASK receiver. Same driver gap: the
  digital input is a host fixture (input-level, sample-rate, samples) and ASK
  demodulation/RF sensitivity/range are NOT RUN.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 m5atoms3r, no guest firmware) attaches glass/rf433t/
rf433r and validates property registration, the glass display-state fixtures
and the rf433 bitstream/input fixtures. The smoke is not a functional PASS and
I2C command-byte semantics, button/buzzer behavior and RF physics still need
guest/hardware evidence.
